                Height 0.09 m keeps the body's original vertical extent, so
                landing height and ground contact are unchanged. -->
           <cylinder>
-            <radius>0.240</radius>
+            <!-- 0.240 -> 0.280. The true swept radius of a QAV-R 2 with 7 in
+                 props is 0.2399 m; 0.280 adds a deliberate 40 mm safety
+                 margin so the SIMULATOR collides EARLIER than the real
+                 aircraft would. A run that clears the arena here therefore
+                 clears it in reality with margin to spare - the error is on
+                 the safe side. Nav2's robot_radius and the explorer's
+                 robot_radius_m are set to the same 0.280; if they ever drift
+                 apart the margin is fictional, because Nav2 would plan paths
+                 the body cannot fit through. -->
+            <radius>0.280</radius>
             <length>0.090</length>
           </cylinder>
         </geometry>
